------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE OF THIS RELEASE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains the technical development and validation code
supporting the publication "Computable longitudinal patient journeys derived
from structured and unstructured EHR data: development, validation, and
clinical application in GLP-1 receptor agonist therapy" (Nature Medicine, 2026):
extraction evaluation, physician adjudication analysis, benchmark comparison,
fine-tuning evaluation and concept-discovery clustering.

The grant in the LICENSE file covers this code only. It does not extend to the
RespondHealth production extraction platform, which is proprietary, is not
distributed here, and is described in the paper's Code availability statement as
unavailable for commercial reasons.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA INCLUDED IN THIS REPOSITORY
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No patient-level electronic health record text is included. The physician
adjudication files record surrogate visit identifiers, extracted term names,
character offsets and reviewer labels; they do not contain the underlying
clinical note text, which is licensed from Harris Computer Systems and cannot be
redistributed. The surrogate visit identifiers exist only to group the three
reviewers' judgements about the same extraction and do not resolve to any record
outside this repository.

The concept-discovery taxonomy in clustering/ records cluster labels, mention
counts and parent groupings. Illustrative note excerpts that accompanied each
cluster in the working copy were removed before publication, on the same
grounds.

